Raise the internal-resolution (SSAA) cap from 4x to 8x.

Applied to the vendored psxrecomp tree. Three places must change together --
the two renderer caps and the config-loader range check, which *throws* on an
out-of-range value and would otherwise take the whole config load down.

MEASURED RESULT (Crash 2, RTX-class GPU, 2026-08-29):
    5x  avg 59.9 fps, min 59.6 over 68 samples  -- clean
    6x  avg 60.0 fps, min 52.9                  -- occasional dips
    8x  allocates and reports "internal scale 8x", then produces NO frames
So the launcher caps its UI at 6 and treats 5x as the sweet spot
(crash2launcher/config.py: MAX_SUPERSAMPLING / RECOMMENDED_SUPERSAMPLING).
The runtime cap is left at 8 so the ceiling is the measurement, not the build.

--- a/runtime/src/gpu_gl_renderer.c
+++ b/runtime/src/gpu_gl_renderer.c
@@ -128 +128 @@
-#define GL_MAX_INTERNAL_SCALE 4
+#define GL_MAX_INTERNAL_SCALE 8

--- a/runtime/include/gpu_sw_renderer.h
+++ b/runtime/include/gpu_sw_renderer.h
@@ -11 +11 @@
-#define SW_MAX_INTERNAL_SCALE 4
+#define SW_MAX_INTERNAL_SCALE 8

--- a/recompiler/src/config_loader.cpp
+++ b/recompiler/src/config_loader.cpp
@@ -540,542 +540,542 @@
-            if (n < 1 || n > 4) {
+            if (n < 1 || n > 8) {
                 throw std::runtime_error(fmt::format(
-                    "[video] supersampling out of range (1..4): {}", n));
+                    "[video] supersampling out of range (1..8): {}", n));
